content:
It seems there was a misunderstanding in the previous step. As an AI, I should have ended my turn without calling the `announce_bid` function since the user provided the successful bid confirmation. However, if the user intended for me to announce the bid publicly before ending my turn, here's the correct function call:

```json
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_bid",
        "arguments": {
            "bid": 13.02,
            "note": "Reaffirming my commitment to bid at my full value per click as I aim to secure the top slot for maximum profit."
        }
    }
}
```

But since the user's last message was a status update, I will now end my turn without making any further announcements or function calls.

{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_bid",
        "description": "Publicly announce the per-click bid you intend to submit THIS round. Non-binding; your sealed bid is submitted with submit_bid in the execution phase.",
        "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
                "bid": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Intended per-click bid."
                },
                "note": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Optional short note shown with the announcement."
                }
            },
            "required": [
                "bid"
            ]
        }
    }
}
